derivations.claim:
[The operators $G(S)$] Fix a Borel $S\subseteq\mathbb R^2$. For fixed $x$, the map $y\mapsto\overline{
u_{x,y}(S)}$ is a bounded linear functional of norm at most $\|x\|$ by step 3.1, so by [F7] there is a unique $G(S)x\in H$ with $\overline{
u_{x,y}(S)}=\langle y,G(S)xangle$, that is $
u_{x,y}(S)=\langle G(S)x,yangle$, and $\|G(S)x\|\le\|x\|$. The assignment $x\mapsto G(S)x$ is linear because the form is linear in its first argument and the representative is unique, so $G(S)\in\mathcal B(H)$ with $\|G(S)\|\le1$; moreover $\langle G(S)x,yangle=
u_{x,y}(S)=\overline{
u_{y,x}(S)}=\overline{\langle G(S)y,xangle}=\langle x,G(S)yangle$, so $G(S)$ is self-adjoint, and $\langle G(S)x,xangle=
u_x(S)\in[0,\|x\|^2]$ gives $0\le G(S)\le I$. [step 3.1, F7, algebra]
